DATA SOURCES (manifest declares useChargingTelemetryLatest; the full web parity also reads location-latest +
  location-history; all bound through the ViewModel as StateFlow from the KMP-core repositories, P1/S8)
  useChargingTelemetryLatest  GET /charging-telemetry/latest [vehicle_id]  → chargingState (web hook name kept
                              at the Kotlin call site: VehiclesRepository.chargingTelemetryLatest).
  location-latest             GET /location-snapshots/latest [vehicle_id]  → latestState.
  location-history            GET /location-snapshots [vehicle_id, limit=200] → historyState (page-local repo).

SI BOUNDARY (P1/S5 / unit-conversion.instructions)
  The wire stays SI: speed_mph is metres-per-second and miles_to_arrival is metres (the legacy field names are
  kept for backward compat — see the web page's SI-floor comment). Display conversion happens only at the render
  boundary via NavDisplayPrefs.toDistanceDisplay (convertDistanceFromSI) / toSpeedDisplay (convertSpeedFromSI) /
  duration (formatDuration) — never stored converted (Phase-48 SI-canonical; ADR-013 keeps the cache SI).

LIVE DATA / STALENESS (ADR-013)
  No SSE live source on this page; the latest/history/charging reads are cache-then-network Resource streams
  (the web page polls via refetchInterval). The header DataFreshness chip surfaces the latest feed's freshness /
  refreshing / stale / error tier (the ADR-013 ">2 min last-known" honest-staleness indicator), driven by
  latestState.fetchedAt/refreshing/stale/hasError.

DATA STATES (the manifest's declared 4: loading → empty → error → success, for every bound source)
  Each panel renders its own loading skeleton / empty state / error-retry / content inline — no region blanks.

